IMPORT prelude

-- Pay-roll Tax Assessment Act 2002 (WA), read with the Pay-roll Tax Act 2002 (WA) and the Pay-roll Tax Assessment
-- Regulations 2003 -- when does my company start paying payroll tax, on what, at what rate, and what must it do first?
--
-- SEAT: the employer-founder (Daniel, for Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd, his company). The Act makes the employer
-- liable (s 7(1)); a founder asks on the company's behalf. Every decision is phrased as he would ask it, from facts he
-- could state about his payroll. Where the Act speaks to the Commissioner (registration, cancellation, exclusion from a
-- group), the encoding says what it means for the employer.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 5 (WA taxable wages); s 6A(1) (wages taxable in this jurisdiction), with ss 6B(1), (4) and 6C(1)
-- read as facts; s 6 (when tax is due); s 7(1), (2) (who is liable; joint and several group liability); s 8 (thresholds
-- and tapering value from 1 July 2020); s 9AA(1) (wages), s 9BA (fringe benefits), s 9CB(1) (superannuation
-- contributions), s 9GA (employment agents), s 9HB (GST excluded); s 10 (annual liability: local nongroup employers,
-- whole and part year) and s 11A; s 17(1)-(5) (annual liability: groups); ss 30, 31(1)-(2), 32(2), 33(1)(a), (2), (3),
-- (4), (5) and 38(1)-(2) (grouping and exclusion); s 24(1), (2), (5) (when I must apply for registration); s 26(1), (3)
-- (monthly returns); Glossary ("employer", "local nongroup employer", "nongroup employer", "Australian taxable wages",
-- "employment agent"). Pay-roll Tax Act 2002 s 5 and Part 3 Table item 1 (the rate). Regulations rr 5-6 (the only
-- prescribed class of contract under s 9AA(1)(c)).
--
-- Edition: Pay-roll Tax Assessment Act 2002 (No. 48 of 2002), WA consolidation as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_42096.txt (retrieved 2026-09-07). Also used: Pay-roll Tax Act 2002 (No. 47 of
-- 2002), as deposited at ../../../pay-roll-tax-act-2002/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_38731.txt (retrieved 2026-09-07);
-- Pay-roll Tax Assessment Regulations 2003, version 03-j0-00 (currency from 1 July 2022), as deposited at
-- ../../../pay-roll-tax-assessment-regulations-2003/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_45213.txt (retrieved 2026-10-20).
--
-- THE FORMULAS ARE MISSING FROM THE DEPOSIT. The deposited text drops the formula images in ss 8(4), 10(2), 10(4),
-- 11A, 12 and 17(3A), (5), leaving only their "where --" glosses. The formulas below are INFERENCES, chosen as the only
-- simple forms consistent with those glosses and with the bands they sit between (each makes the deductable amount nil
-- exactly at the upper threshold, where s 10(1)(b) takes over). They must be checked against the gazetted text.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: interstate nongroup employers (ss 13-16); progressive monthly liability (ss 11, 12, 15, 19) and annual
-- reconciliation (ss 16, 20); the 2019-20 half-year rules (s 7A, Part 2 Division 6) and the sliding scale rates of
-- 2018-2023 above item 1 (Pay-roll Tax Act ss 6-11); the valuation detail of fringe benefits (ss 9BB-9BI: the value is an
-- input), superannuation (ss 9CC, 9CD), shares and options (Subdiv 4), termination payments (s 9EA), allowances (ss 9FA,
-- 9FB), wages in kind (s 9HA) and third parties (s 9HC); s 6A(2)-(8) month rules and ss 6B, 6C, 6D in detail (their
-- outcomes are asked as facts); tax-reducing arrangements (s 21); tracing through corporations and trusts (ss 34, 35A-37);
-- the DGE (s 39); the exempt wages of Part 5 (asked as a fact); exemption from monthly returns (s 29, reg 48);
-- charities and beneficial bodies (ss 41-42C); machinery (ss 1-4, 5A, 25(2C), 43-46, Schedule 1). Borrowed terms asked
-- as facts: employee, related bodies corporate, fringe benefit and exempt benefit (FBTA Act), GST, ABN.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice.
-- Judgments the Act hands to the Commissioner are INPUTS ("if the Commissioner is satisfied that ...").

§ `Pay-roll Tax Assessment Act 2002`

§§ `s 9AA, s 9BA, s 9CB, s 9GA, s 9HB, regs 5-6 -- what counts as wages`

-- s 9AA(1): "wages means -- (a) wages, remuneration, salary, commission, bonuses or allowances paid or payable to or in
-- relation to an employee; and (b) an amount paid or payable by way of remuneration to a person holding an office under,
-- or in the service of, the Crown in right of the State of Western Australia; and (c) an amount paid or payable under a
-- contract in a class of contract prescribed under section 45(2)(g), to the extent to which that payment is attributable
-- to labour; and (d) an amount paid or payable by a company by way of remuneration to or in relation to a director of that
-- company; and (e) an amount paid or payable by way of commission to an insurance or timepayment canvasser or collector;
-- and (f) an amount that is taken to be wages ... by another provision of this Division ..."
-- s 9BA(1): "The value of a fringe benefit or a specified taxable benefit that is provided by an employer to or in relation
-- to an employee is taken to be wages ..." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to benefits that are exempt benefits for the
-- purposes of the FBTA Act."
-- s 9CB(1): "a superannuation contribution made by an employer in respect of an employee in a return period" is "taken to
-- be wages paid by the employer to the employee in the return period".
-- s 9GA: an amount paid by an employment agent to a person "engaged to perform the services for a client of the
-- employment agent" is "taken to be wages paid or payable by the agent (as an employer)".
-- Reg 5: an amount is wages under s 9AA(1)(c) "if the amount is paid or payable under a contract made between a ship or
-- boat builder and another party for the procurement of the services of persons to provide solely or mainly labour for
-- all or any of the design, construction, fit-out or maintenance of a ship or boat." Reg 6 excludes "(a) a contract to
-- produce a given result for a fixed fee; or (b) a contract covered by an industrial award; or (c) [a workplace
-- agreement]; or (d) [an employer-employee agreement]; or (e)" a contract to which a registered employer, liable for
-- payroll tax on what it pays the labourers, is a party.
-- s 9HB(1): wages relating to a supply on which the payee is liable to pay GST are reduced "by the amount of GST payable";
-- (2): not for "the value of wages comprising a fringe benefit".
-- Plain gloss: wages are what an employer pays its employees and directors, in money or in kind, plus super and fringe
-- benefits. A payment to an independent contractor is not wages under this Act unless it falls in the one prescribed
-- class (ship and boat building labour contracts) or comes through an employment agent.
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `wages, salary, commission, bonus or allowance to an employee`
    `remuneration to a holder of an office under the WA Crown`
    `remuneration by the company to one of its directors`
    `commission to an insurance or time-payment canvasser or collector`
    `a superannuation contribution for an employee`
    `a fringe benefit or specified taxable benefit for an employee`
    `a payment to an independent contractor`
    `a payment by me as an employment agent to a worker I placed with a client`
    `something else`

DECLARE `My payment` HAS
    `kind` IS A `Kind of payment`
    @desc What the payment is
    `amount` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The amount paid or payable, in dollars; for a fringe benefit, its value under ss 9BB-9BI
    `the contract is a ship or boat builder's contract procuring persons to provide mainly labour` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc For a contractor: whether the contract is between a ship or boat builder and another party for persons to provide solely or mainly labour for the design, construction, fit-out or maintenance of a ship or boat (reg 5)
    `the contract is excluded by regulation 6` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc For a contractor: whether the contract is for a given result for a fixed fee, covered by an award or a workplace or employer-employee agreement, or one where a registered employer pays tax on the labour (reg 6)
    `part attributable to labour` IS A NUMBER
    @desc For a contractor: the part of the amount attributable to labour, in dollars
    `the benefit is an exempt benefit under the FBTA Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc For a fringe benefit: whether it is an exempt benefit for FBT purposes
    `GST the payee must pay on it` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The GST the payee is liable to pay on the supply the payment relates to, in dollars (nil if none)
    `it is exempt wages under Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether Part 5 of the Act exempts it (for example parental leave pay, apprentices under training contracts)

GIVEN `the payment` IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount before GST is taken out` IS
    CONSIDER `the payment`'s `kind`
    WHEN `wages, salary, commission, bonus or allowance to an employee` THEN `the payment`'s `amount`
    WHEN `remuneration to a holder of an office under the WA Crown` THEN `the payment`'s `amount`
    WHEN `remuneration by the company to one of its directors` THEN `the payment`'s `amount`
    WHEN `commission to an insurance or time-payment canvasser or collector` THEN `the payment`'s `amount`
    WHEN `a superannuation contribution for an employee` THEN `the payment`'s `amount`
    WHEN `a fringe benefit or specified taxable benefit for an employee` THEN
        IF `the payment`'s `the benefit is an exempt benefit under the FBTA Act` THEN 0 ELSE `the payment`'s `amount`
    WHEN `a payment to an independent contractor` THEN
        IF     `the payment`'s `the contract is a ship or boat builder's contract procuring persons to provide mainly labour`
           AND (NOT (`the payment`'s `the contract is excluded by regulation 6`))
        THEN `the payment`'s `part attributable to labour`
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `a payment by me as an employment agent to a worker I placed with a client` THEN `the payment`'s `amount`
    WHEN `something else` THEN 0

@export How much of this payment counts as wages for payroll tax (ss 9AA, 9BA, 9CB, 9GA, 9HB; regs 5-6)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `My payment` @desc The payment and what it is for
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of this payment is wages` IS
    IF `the payment`'s `kind` EQUALS `a fringe benefit or specified taxable benefit for an employee`
    THEN `the amount before GST is taken out` `the payment`
    ELSE IF `the amount before GST is taken out` `the payment` GREATER THAN `the payment`'s `GST the payee must pay on it`
         THEN `the amount before GST is taken out` `the payment` MINUS `the payment`'s `GST the payee must pay on it`
         ELSE 0

@export Is this payment wages for payroll tax (s 9AA)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `My payment` @desc The payment and what it is for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this payment wages` IF
    `How much of this payment is wages` `the payment` GREATER THAN 0

§§ `ss 5 and 6A -- which wages are WA taxable wages`

-- s 5(2): "WA taxable wages are wages, other than exempt wages, that are taxable in this jurisdiction."
-- s 6A(1): wages are taxable in this jurisdiction if "(a) ... for or in relation to services performed by a person wholly
-- in this jurisdiction; or (b) ... services performed by a person in 2 or more Australian jurisdictions, or partly in one or
-- more Australian jurisdictions and partly outside all Australian jurisdictions, and -- (i) the person is based in this
-- jurisdiction; or (ii) the employer is based in this jurisdiction -- in a case where the person is not based in an
-- Australian jurisdiction; or (iii) the wages are paid or payable in this jurisdiction -- in a case where both the person
-- and the employer are not based in an Australian jurisdiction; or (iv) the wages are paid or payable for services
-- performed mainly in this jurisdiction -- in a case where both the person and employer are not based in an Australian
-- jurisdiction and the wages are not paid or payable in an Australian jurisdiction; or (c) ... services performed by a
-- person wholly outside all Australian jurisdictions and are paid or payable in this jurisdiction."
-- s 6B(1): a person is based where their "principal place of residence is located"; s 6C(1): an employer is based where
-- its ABN registered business address is (or, without an ABN, its principal place of business). Both are asked as facts.
-- Plain gloss: work done in WA is taxed in WA; work spread across States is taxed where the worker lives.
DECLARE `Where the services were done in the month` IS ONE OF
    `wholly in WA`
    `wholly in one other State or Territory`
    `in 2 or more States or Territories, or partly in Australia and partly overseas`
    `wholly outside Australia`

DECLARE `Place` IS ONE OF
    `in WA`
    `in another State or Territory`
    `not in any State or Territory`

DECLARE `Where the work was done and paid` HAS
    `services` IS A `Where the services were done in the month`
    @desc Where the worker performed the services during the month the wages were paid or payable (s 6A(2))
    `the worker is based` IS A `Place`
    @desc Where the worker's principal place of residence was in that month (s 6B)
    `the employer is based` IS A `Place`
    @desc Where your registered business address (or principal place of business) was in that month (s 6C)
    `the wages were paid or payable` IS A `Place`
    @desc Where the wages were paid or payable (s 6D)
    `the services were done mainly in WA` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the services were performed mainly in WA

@export Are these wages taxable in WA (s 6A(1))?
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Where the work was done and paid` @desc Where the work was done and paid in the month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the wages taxable in WA` IF
    CONSIDER `the work`'s `services`
    WHEN `wholly in WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `wholly in one other State or Territory` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in 2 or more States or Territories, or partly in Australia and partly overseas` THEN
            `the work`'s `the worker is based` EQUALS `in WA`
        OR  (    `the work`'s `the worker is based` EQUALS `not in any State or Territory`
             AND `the work`'s `the employer is based` EQUALS `in WA`)
        OR  (    `the work`'s `the worker is based` EQUALS `not in any State or Territory`
             AND `the work`'s `the employer is based` EQUALS `not in any State or Territory`
             AND `the work`'s `the wages were paid or payable` EQUALS `in WA`)
        OR  (    `the work`'s `the worker is based` EQUALS `not in any State or Territory`
             AND `the work`'s `the employer is based` EQUALS `not in any State or Territory`
             AND `the work`'s `the wages were paid or payable` EQUALS `not in any State or Territory`
             AND `the work`'s `the services were done mainly in WA`)
    WHEN `wholly outside Australia` THEN `the work`'s `the wages were paid or payable` EQUALS `in WA`

@export How much of this payment is WA taxable wages (s 5(2))?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `My payment` @desc The payment and what it is for
      `the work` IS A `Where the work was done and paid` @desc Where the work was done and paid in the month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages` IS
    IF     `Are the wages taxable in WA` `the work`
       AND (NOT (`the payment`'s `it is exempt wages under Part 5`))
    THEN `How much of this payment is wages` `the payment`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Part 4 -- am I in a group`

-- s 30: "corporations constitute a group if they are related bodies corporate."
-- s 31(1): "An employer and another person ... constitute a group if one or more of the employer's employees performs
-- duties solely or mainly for or in connection with one or more businesses carried on by the employer and the other
-- person ..., or carried on by the other person ..." (2): likewise if the employer has "an agreement, arrangement or
-- undertaking" with the other person about their business that "relates to the employment of, or the performance of
-- duties by, one or more of the employer's employees".
-- s 32(2): "If the same person has, or the same persons have together, a controlling interest in each of 2 businesses, the
-- persons who carry on those businesses constitute a group."
-- s 33: a controlling interest in a business carried on by a corporation is held by a director entitled "to exercise more
-- than 50% of the voting power at meetings of the directors" (1)(a), or by one who may exercise or control "more than 50%
-- of the voting power attached to voting shares" (2); in a partnership, "more than 50% of the capital" or "more than 50%
-- of any profits" (3); in a trust, "a beneficial interest in respect of more than 50% of the value of the interests" (4);
-- and the "sole owner of the business" has one (5).
-- s 38(1): the Commissioner "may ... exclude a person from a group under section 31(4), 32(3), 35A(4) or 36(4) ... if
-- satisfied that the business is carried on independently of, and is not connected with" the others' businesses.
-- (2): "a corporation cannot be excluded from a group if it and another corporation which is a member of the group are
-- related bodies corporate."
-- Plain gloss: businesses under common control, or sharing staff, pay as one: one threshold between them.
DECLARE `A person's hold on a business` HAS
    `share of voting power on voting shares` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The percentage of the voting power attached to voting shares the person (with any others acting with them) can exercise or control
    `share of directors' votes as a director` IS A NUMBER
    @desc If the person is a director, the percentage of the voting power at directors' meetings they can exercise
    `share of partnership capital` IS A NUMBER
    @desc For a partnership: the percentage of its capital the person owns
    `share of partnership profits` IS A NUMBER
    @desc For a partnership: the percentage of its profits the person is entitled to
    `share of the value of interests in the trust` IS A NUMBER
    @desc For a trust: the percentage of the value of the interests in the trust the person holds beneficially
    `is the sole owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the person is the sole owner of the business

@export Does this person hold a controlling interest in the business (s 33)?
GIVEN `the hold` IS A `A person's hold on a business` @desc How the person holds the business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the person hold a controlling interest` IF
        `the hold`'s `share of voting power on voting shares` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `the hold`'s `share of directors' votes as a director` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `the hold`'s `share of partnership capital` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `the hold`'s `share of partnership profits` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `the hold`'s `share of the value of interests in the trust` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `the hold`'s `is the sole owner`

DECLARE `My business and another` HAS
    `we are related bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether my company and the other are related bodies corporate (Corporations Act s 9)
    `one of my employees works solely or mainly for the other business` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether an employee of mine performs duties solely or mainly for or in connection with a business the other person carries on (alone or with me)
    `I have an arrangement with the other about my employees' work` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether I have an agreement, arrangement or undertaking with the other about their business that relates to the employment or duties of my employees
    `the common person's hold on my business` IS A `A person's hold on a business`
    @desc How the person (or persons) who hold both hold my business
    `the common person's hold on the other business` IS A `A person's hold on a business`
    @desc How the same person (or persons) hold the other business
    `the Commissioner has excluded me from the group` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Commissioner, satisfied my business is carried on independently of and unconnected with the other's, has excluded me by written notice (s 38)

@export Is my business grouped with the other business for payroll tax (ss 30-33, 38)?
GIVEN `the two` IS A `My business and another` @desc My business and the other business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I grouped with the other business` IF
        `the two`'s `we are related bodies corporate`
    OR  (    (    `the two`'s `one of my employees works solely or mainly for the other business`
              OR  `the two`'s `I have an arrangement with the other about my employees' work`
              OR  (    `Does the person hold a controlling interest` (`the two`'s `the common person's hold on my business`)
                   AND `Does the person hold a controlling interest` (`the two`'s `the common person's hold on the other business`)))
         AND (NOT (`the two`'s `the Commissioner has excluded me from the group`)))

-- s 7(2): "Payroll tax payable on wages by a member or members of a group is a debt due jointly and severally by each
-- person who is a member of the group during the period in which the wages become payable." (3): this "does not affect the
-- liability of an employer under subsection (1)".
@export Can I be made to pay payroll tax owed on another group member's wages (s 7(2))?
GIVEN `I was a member of the group when those wages became payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a member of the group during the period in which the wages became payable
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to pay the group's payroll tax` IF
    `I was a member of the group when those wages became payable`

§§ `s 8 -- the thresholds`

-- s 8: "(1) The annual threshold amount for a financial year beginning on or after 1 July 2020 is $1 000 000. (2) The
-- monthly threshold amount ... is $83 333. (3) The upper threshold amount ... is $7 500 000. (4) The tapering value ... is
-- to be calculated as follows -- [formula missing from deposit] where -- AT is the annual threshold amount for the year;
-- UT is the upper threshold amount for the year."
-- INFERENCE (formula image not deposited): tapering value = AT / (UT - AT).
-- Plain gloss: the first $1 million a year is free of tax; the free amount shrinks as wages rise, and is gone at $7.5
-- million.
@export What is the annual threshold amount (s 8(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the annual threshold amount` IS 1000000

@export What is the monthly threshold amount (s 8(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly threshold amount` IS 83333

@export What is the upper threshold amount (s 8(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the upper threshold amount` IS 7500000

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the tapering value` IS
    `the annual threshold amount` DIVIDED BY (`the upper threshold amount` MINUS `the annual threshold amount`)

§ `Pay-roll Tax Act 2002 -- the rate`

-- Pay-roll Tax Act s 5: "(1) Payroll tax on wages paid or payable before 1 January 2005 is imposed at the rate of 6%. (2)
-- ... during the period that begins on 1 January 2005 and ends on 30 June 2018 is imposed at the rate of 5.5%. (3) ...
-- during the period that begins on 1 July 2018 and ends on 30 June 2023 (the sliding scale period) is imposed at the rates
-- determined under" Part 3. "(4) Payroll tax on wages paid or payable on or after 1 July 2023 is imposed at the rate of
-- 5.5%."
-- Part 3 ss 6(1), 10(2), Table item 1: wages "Not more than $100 000 000 x Y": 5.5%; where Y is the fraction of the
-- assessment year in which wages were paid or payable. Items 2 and 3 use formulas missing from the deposit.
-- The assessment year is named by the calendar year in which it ends (2031-32 is 2032).
DECLARE `My payroll tax rate` IS ONE OF
    `5.5 per cent`
    `not encoded: a sliding scale rate above Table item 1`

@export What payroll tax rate applies to my assessment year (Pay-roll Tax Act s 5)?
GIVEN `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessment year, named by the calendar year in which it ends (2031-32 is 2032)
      `wages for the rate table` IS A NUMBER @desc Your WA taxable wages for the year (for a group, the group's Australian taxable wages)
      `fraction of the year with wages` IS A NUMBER @desc The days in the year on which wages were paid or payable, divided by the days in the year (1 for a whole year)
GIVETH A `My payroll tax rate`
DECIDE `What is my payroll tax rate` IS
    IF `the assessment year` AT LEAST 2024
    THEN `5.5 per cent`
    ELSE IF `wages for the rate table` AT MOST 100000000 TIMES `fraction of the year with wages`
         THEN `5.5 per cent`
         ELSE `not encoded: a sliding scale rate above Table item 1`

§ `Pay-roll Tax Assessment Act 2002 -- how much I pay`

§§ `ss 10 and 11A -- a local nongroup employer`

-- Glossary: "nongroup employer means an employer who is not a member of a group under Part 4"; "local nongroup employer
-- means a nongroup employer who pays or is liable to pay WA taxable wages during part or all of an assessment year, but is
-- not liable to pay any interstate taxable wages during the assessment year".
-- s 10(1): for a whole year, the tax is "(a) if the total amount of WA taxable wages ... is less than or equal to the
-- annual threshold amount for the year -- nil; (b) if [it] is equal to or greater than the upper threshold amount for the
-- year -- the amount calculated by applying the payroll tax rate to the total amount of WA taxable wages ...; (c) otherwise
-- -- ... the payroll tax rate [applied] to ... the difference between -- (i) the total amount of WA taxable wages ...; and
-- (ii) the deductable amount ..." (2): the deductable amount "[formula missing from deposit] where -- AT is the annual
-- threshold amount ...; TV is the tapering value ...; W is the total amount of WA taxable wages".
-- (3), (4): the same for a part-year, with the apportioned annual and upper threshold amounts, "TV is the tapering value
-- for the year". s 11A(1), (2): AT and UT apportioned with "P is the number of days in that part of the year; Y is the
-- number of days in the year" [formulas missing from deposit].
-- INFERENCES (formula images not deposited): deductable amount = AT - ((W - AT) x TV); apportioned amount = amount x P / Y.
DECLARE `Which band I am in` IS ONE OF
    `nil: my wages are at or below the threshold`
    `tapered: tax on my wages less the deductable amount`
    `full: tax on all my wages, at or above the upper threshold`
    `not encoded: this assessment year`

DECLARE `My year as a local nongroup employer` HAS
    `assessment year` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The assessment year, named by the calendar year in which it ends (2031-32 is 2032)
    `WA taxable wages` IS A NUMBER
    @desc Your total WA taxable wages paid or payable in the year (or part-year), in dollars
    `days I was a local nongroup employer` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The days in the year on which you were a local nongroup employer (all of them for a whole year)
    `days in the year` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The days in the assessment year (365 or 366)

GIVEN `the year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the fraction of the year` IS
    `the year`'s `days I was a local nongroup employer` DIVIDED BY `the year`'s `days in the year`

@export What is my annual threshold, apportioned if I was a local nongroup employer for part of the year (ss 10, 11A(1))?
GIVEN `the year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer` @desc Your year as an employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my threshold for the year` IS
    `the annual threshold amount` TIMES `the fraction of the year` `the year`

GIVEN `the year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `my upper threshold for the year` IS
    `the upper threshold amount` TIMES `the fraction of the year` `the year`

@export Which band of s 10 am I in for the year?
GIVEN `the year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer` @desc Your year as an employer
GIVETH A `Which band I am in`
DECIDE `Which band am I in` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year`'s `assessment year` LESS THAN 2021
            THEN `not encoded: this assessment year`
        IF NOT (`What is my payroll tax rate` (`the year`'s `assessment year`) (`the year`'s `WA taxable wages`) (`the fraction of the year` `the year`) EQUALS `5.5 per cent`)
            THEN `not encoded: this assessment year`
        IF `the year`'s `WA taxable wages` AT MOST `What is my threshold for the year` `the year`
            THEN `nil: my wages are at or below the threshold`
        IF `the year`'s `WA taxable wages` AT LEAST `my upper threshold for the year` `the year`
            THEN `full: tax on all my wages, at or above the upper threshold`
        OTHERWISE `tapered: tax on my wages less the deductable amount`

@export What is my deductable amount for the year (s 10(2), (4))?
GIVEN `the year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer` @desc Your year as an employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my deductable amount` IS
    `What is my threshold for the year` `the year`
    MINUS ((`the year`'s `WA taxable wages` MINUS `What is my threshold for the year` `the year`) TIMES `the tapering value`)

-- -1 is returned, and means "not encoded", for an assessment year before 2020-21 or a sliding scale rate above item 1.
@export How much payroll tax must my company pay for the year (s 10)?
GIVEN `the year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer` @desc Your year as an employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` IS
    CONSIDER `Which band am I in` `the year`
    WHEN `nil: my wages are at or below the threshold` THEN 0
    WHEN `full: tax on all my wages, at or above the upper threshold` THEN `the year`'s `WA taxable wages` TIMES 0.055
    WHEN `tapered: tax on my wages less the deductable amount` THEN
        (`the year`'s `WA taxable wages` MINUS `What is my deductable amount` `the year`) TIMES 0.055
    WHEN `not encoded: this assessment year` THEN -1

@export Does my company pay any payroll tax for the year (s 10)?
GIVEN `the year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer` @desc Your year as an employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my company pay payroll tax for the year` IF
    `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` `the year` GREATER THAN 0

§§ `s 17 -- a group`

-- s 17(2): for a group with a member paying Australian taxable wages at all times in the year, the tax is "(a) if the
-- total amount of Australian taxable wages paid or payable by the group members during the year is less than or equal to
-- the annual threshold amount for the year -- nil; (b) if [that total] is equal to or greater than the upper threshold
-- amount for the year -- the amount calculated by applying the payroll tax rate to the total amount of WA taxable wages
-- paid or payable by the group members during the year; (c) otherwise -- ... the payroll tax rate [applied to] the
-- difference between -- (i) the total amount of WA taxable wages ...; and (ii) the deductable amount for the group". (3A):
-- "[formula missing from deposit] where -- AT is the annual threshold amount ...; TW is the total amount of Australian
-- taxable wages ...; TV is the tapering value ...; W is the total amount of WA taxable wages". Glossary: "Australian
-- taxable wages means WA taxable wages and interstate taxable wages".
-- INFERENCE (formula image not deposited): deductable amount = (W / TW) x (AT - ((TW - AT) x TV)).
-- Plain gloss: the group tests its Australia-wide wages against one threshold, and pays WA tax on its WA share.
-- The part-year case (s 17(3)-(7)) is not encoded.
DECLARE `My group's year` HAS
    `assessment year` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The assessment year, named by the calendar year in which it ends
    `the group's Australian taxable wages` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The total WA and interstate taxable wages of all group members in the year, in dollars
    `the group's WA taxable wages` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The total WA taxable wages of all group members in the year, in dollars

@export Which band of s 17 is my group in for the year?
GIVEN `the group` IS A `My group's year` @desc The group's wages for the year
GIVETH A `Which band I am in`
DECIDE `Which band is my group in` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the group`'s `assessment year` LESS THAN 2021
            THEN `not encoded: this assessment year`
        IF NOT (`What is my payroll tax rate` (`the group`'s `assessment year`) (`the group`'s `the group's Australian taxable wages`) 1 EQUALS `5.5 per cent`)
            THEN `not encoded: this assessment year`
        IF `the group`'s `the group's Australian taxable wages` AT MOST `the annual threshold amount`
            THEN `nil: my wages are at or below the threshold`
        IF `the group`'s `the group's Australian taxable wages` AT LEAST `the upper threshold amount`
            THEN `full: tax on all my wages, at or above the upper threshold`
        OTHERWISE `tapered: tax on my wages less the deductable amount`

@export What is my group's deductable amount for the year (s 17(3A))?
GIVEN `the group` IS A `My group's year` @desc The group's wages for the year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my group's deductable amount` IS
    (`the group`'s `the group's WA taxable wages` DIVIDED BY `the group`'s `the group's Australian taxable wages`)
    TIMES (`the annual threshold amount`
           MINUS ((`the group`'s `the group's Australian taxable wages` MINUS `the annual threshold amount`) TIMES `the tapering value`))

-- -1 is returned, and means "not encoded", for an assessment year before 2020-21 or a sliding scale rate above item 1.
@export How much WA payroll tax must my group pay for the year (s 17(2))?
GIVEN `the group` IS A `My group's year` @desc The group's wages for the year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much payroll tax must my group pay for the year` IS
    CONSIDER `Which band is my group in` `the group`
    WHEN `nil: my wages are at or below the threshold` THEN 0
    WHEN `full: tax on all my wages, at or above the upper threshold` THEN `the group`'s `the group's WA taxable wages` TIMES 0.055
    WHEN `tapered: tax on my wages less the deductable amount` THEN
        (`the group`'s `the group's WA taxable wages` MINUS `What is my group's deductable amount` `the group`) TIMES 0.055
    WHEN `not encoded: this assessment year` THEN -1

§ `Part 3 -- registration and returns`

§§ `s 24 -- must I register`

-- s 24(1): "A nongroup employer who is not registered must apply to the Commissioner for registration if -- (a) the
-- employer pays or is liable to pay any WA taxable wages during a month; and (b) the total amount of the WA taxable wages
-- and any interstate taxable wages that the employer pays or is liable to pay during the month exceeds the monthly
-- threshold amount. Penalty: a fine of $20 000." (2): "A group member who is not registered must apply for registration if
-- the member pays or is liable to pay any WA taxable wages during a month. Penalty: a fine of $20 000." (5): "An
-- application under subsection (1) or (2) must be made to the Commissioner within 7 days after the end of the month."
-- s 25(1): the Commissioner "must register the applicant ... if it appears to the Commissioner that the employer is, or is
-- likely to become, liable to pay payroll tax." (2A): the Commissioner may register an employer who has not applied.
-- Plain gloss: a stand-alone employer registers once a month's wages pass $83,333; a group member registers as soon as it
-- pays any WA wages.
DECLARE `My month` HAS
    `I am registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are already registered as an employer under s 25
    `I am a member of a group` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are a member of a group under Part 4
    `WA taxable wages in the month` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The WA taxable wages you paid or were liable to pay in the month, in dollars
    `interstate taxable wages in the month` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The wages taxable under another State's or Territory's payroll tax law that you paid or were liable to pay in the month, in dollars
    `the month` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The month, 1 (January) to 12 (December)

@export Must my company apply to register for payroll tax (s 24(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the month` IS A `My month` @desc Your wages in a month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to register for payroll tax` IF
        (NOT (`the month`'s `I am registered`))
    AND `the month`'s `WA taxable wages in the month` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (    `the month`'s `I am a member of a group`
         OR  `the month`'s `WA taxable wages in the month` PLUS `the month`'s `interstate taxable wages in the month`
                 GREATER THAN `the monthly threshold amount`)

@export How many days after the end of the month do I have to apply for registration (s 24(5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days after the month do I have to apply` IS 7

@export What is the most I can be fined for not applying for registration (s 24(1), (2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not registering` IS 20000

§§ `ss 26 and 6 -- monthly returns, and when tax is due`

-- s 26(1): "An employer who is registered or required to apply for registration under section 24 must lodge a return for
-- each month specifying the amount of the WA taxable wages ..., unless the employer is exempted under section 29." (3): "(a)
-- for a month other than June -- be lodged within 7 days after the end of the month ...; and (b) for June -- be lodged
-- within 21 days after the end of the month, or within any further time allowed by the Commissioner in a particular case.
-- Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
-- s 6: "Payroll tax is due for payment on the last day for lodging the return of the wages on which the payroll tax is
-- payable."
@export Must my company lodge a monthly return (s 26(1))?
GIVEN `the month` IS A `My month` @desc Your wages in a month
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from monthly returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an exemption under s 29
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge a monthly return` IF
        (`the month`'s `I am registered` OR `Must I apply to register for payroll tax` `the month`)
    AND (NOT `the Commissioner has exempted me from monthly returns`)

@export How many days after the end of the month do I have to lodge the return and pay the tax (ss 26(3), 6)?
GIVEN `the month` IS A `My month` @desc Your wages in a month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days after the month do I have to lodge and pay` IS
    IF `the month`'s `the month` EQUALS 6 THEN 21 ELSE 7

@export What is the most I can be fined for not lodging a monthly return in time (s 26(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for a late return` IS 5000
